SWEET WLAN stage 1 (patch 0128): READ-ONLY attach of the BCM4389 from inside XNU (docs/research/42, W-D2). Inert unless boot-arg sweetwlan=1|2 AND ADT /sweet-wlan
(tools/mkadt.py, bluejay only) AND the PCIe1 link left up by the shim flavor --wlan-hold. bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_chip.h = OpenBSD bwfm.c EROM walk (ISC) + the
BAR0 read allowlist of shim/wlanlink.c mem_ok(); bsd/dev/sweet_wlan.c = ADT/precheck/mapping glue. The only write is the BAR0 window select (cfg 0x80).
Host test: shim/wlan_xnu_host_test.c. Hardware-reading path: reviewed in docs/reviews (see the commit).

